<description>
Recolor the largest rectangular black pocket(s) in each black component red.

Input structure
- The input is a grey field with black empty regions; no red pixels are
  present initially.
- Black regions are interpreted as 4-connected components.
- Some black components contain a solid rectangular subregion with both
  height and width at least 2.

Rule
- For each 4-connected black component, enumerate all solid all-black
  rectangles with height >= 2 and width >= 2.
- If a component contains such rectangles, recolor every maximum-area
  rectangle in that component to red.
- Leave grey pixels and black cells outside those selected rectangles
  unchanged.

Key insight
- The output is not the union of every black 2x2 square; within each black
  component, smaller overlapping rectangles are ignored unless they tie for
  the largest area.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "4-connected black components on a grey field",
  "transform": "within each component, find all solid black rectangles with height and width at least 2; recolor every maximum-area rectangle red, including ties, and leave all other pixels unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 18x18 [observed]
  colors: grey (background) and black (foreground); no red in input
  black_density: 0.36-0.45 of all cells
  black_components: 32-46 4-connected components per grid
  component_types:
    qualifying: 3-5 per grid; size 6-17 cells; bbox 2x4 to 5x5;
      contains exactly one max solid rectangle with h>=2 and w>=2 (area 4-8);
      may have 1-2 tied max rects (1 comp in 1 example had 2 ties, rest had 1);
      remaining cells form thin arms/branches around the rectangle
    non_qualifying: 28-43 per grid; size 1-16 cells;
      must NOT contain any 2x2 solid black sub-block;
      mostly size 1-3 (single cells, pairs, thin L-shapes);
      a few larger ones (size 5-16) are thin snaking/branching paths
  transform: for each qualifying component, recolor its max-area solid rectangle(s) red
  total_red_cells: 16-24 per grid

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first with embedded rectangles
  steps:
    1. Start with an 18x18 all-grey grid.
    2. Place 3-5 qualifying components. For each, first place a solid black
       rectangle (2x2 to 4x2 or 2x3), then grow 2-6 thin black arms (width-1
       paths, no 2x2 blocks) from its edges. Total component size 6-17.
       Record rectangle positions for the output.
    3. Fill remaining grid area with random black noise at ~35-45% density,
       but ensure no new 2x2 all-black block is created. Use rejection per cell
       or iterative placement checking the 2x2 neighborhood constraint.
    4. The noise creates many small non-qualifying components (size 1-5) plus
       occasional larger thin components, matching observed distributions.
    5. Output = input with qualifying rectangles recolored red.
```
